# WordPress, asked what its entrypoint starts: apache. The package is as far as this goes, and the
# reason is in the image rather than in the package. The php image turns apache to prefork, since
# mod_php wants it, and in prefork the master serves nothing: the workers do, and they are made with
# fork. glibc asks for that with a clone that does not share the address space, which nanos answers
# with ENOSYS, so the master listens on 80 and accepts nothing for as long as it is left running.
# wordpress-php is the same application in a shape a unikernel can run.
DOCKERFILE=../wordpress/Dockerfile
EXPECT=package
BUILD_FLAGS="--resolve-entrypoint --resolve-timeout 120"
MANIFEST_CHECK='(.Program | test("apache2$"))'
